WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Separation and wake. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Explain pressure-gradient effects

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: An adverse pressure gradient can contribute to boundary-layer separation. The resulting wake affects forces, but its exact shape needs evidence.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Sketch attached flow, then a separated region; label this as a conceptual diagram, not measured CFD.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Cause-and-effect diagram

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Simplified flow picture; real values need test method and conditions.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Explain pressure-gradient effects
